# Acceptance fixtures are byte-exact inputs, not text to be tidied.
#
# Two of them encode a parser assumption in their bytes: linkedin-connections.csv
# and excel-de.csv ship CRLF, and excel-de.csv is Windows-1252, not UTF-8. Git's
# default eol normalisation (any clone with core.autocrlf set) would rewrite both,
# and the encoding and preamble tests would then pass for the wrong reason.
#
# -text disables eol conversion while keeping the files diffable.
fixtures/** -text
